 THE PROPERTY DESCRIBED IN THIS INSTRUMENT MAY NOT BE WITHIN A FIRE PROTECTION DISTRICT PROTECTING STRUCTURES.  THE PROPERTY IS SUBJECT TO LAND USE LAWS AND REGULATION, WHICH, IN FARM OR FOREST ZONES, MAY NOT AUTHORIZE CONSTRUCTION OR SITING OF A RESIDENCE AND WHICH LIMIT LAWSUITS AGAINST FARMING OR FOREST PRACTICES AS DEFINED IN ORS 30.930 IN ALL ZONES.  BEFORE SIGNING OR ACCEPTING THIS INSTRUMENT, THE PERSON ACQUIRING FEE TITLE OF THE PROPERTY SHOULD CHECK WITH THE APPROPRIATE CITY OR COUNTY PLANNING DEPARTMENT TO VERIFY APPROVED USES AND EXISTENCE OF FIRE PROTECTION FOR STRUCTURES.

 SELLER represents:(1)that he knows of no material structural defects;(2)that he has no notice of any liens to be assessed against the property; (3) the parties acknowledge that the property may be subject to City, County or State Smoke Detector requirements.

 All built-in appliances, wall to wall carpeting, draperies and curtain/ blinds, curtain rods, window and door screens, storm doors and windows, all irrigation, plumbing, ventilating, cooling and heating fixtures and equipment (including stoker and oil tanks but excluding detached fireplace equipment), water heater, attached electrical lights and bathroom fixtures, light bulbs, fluorescent lamps, venetian blinds, awnings, attached linoleum, attached television antenna, all planted shrubs, and trees are to be left upon the premises as part of the property purchased.

 Subject sale will be closed in escrow, the cost to be borne by equally  by the parties hereto.  Prorates of taxes, interest and fires insurance premiums (if the PURCHASER assumes existing policy) and other prepaid expenses attributable to the property, are to be made as of possession.  PURCHASER may elect to provide a new insurance policy.  Rents to be prorated as of closing.  Transaction is to be closed as soon as financing documents can be prepared and marketable title is delivered. 

 Closing shall occur no later than November 30, 2001.  Time of performance being made strictly of the essence.

TIME IS OF THE ESSENCE OF THIS AGREEMENT.  Possession shall be delivered to PURCHASER: one day after recording of the above mentioned deed or contract, or as soon thereafter as existing laws and regulations will permit removal of tenants, if any; The sale will be closed in escrow at                                (The Escrow).

 CONTINGENCIES.  This agreement is subject to septic approval for a single family residence utilizing the easement referred to hereinabove for such purposes.  PURCHASER shall arrange for the septic test as soon as reasonably possible after acceptance by SELLER.  This agreement is also subject to PURCHASER confirming that zoning laws and ordinances will allow the demolition of the existing structure on the property and the construction of a new single family dwelling on the premises.  Not later than the date septic is approved, PURCHASER shall complete all inquires regarding this contingency.  In the event the property fails to obtain standard septic approval and/or the zoning laws prohibit the placement  of a new single family dwelling on the premises, PURCHASER shall provide SELLER written notice of the failure of said contingency within ten days of learning of said failure. 

 OPTION.  At closing, and in addition to a deed on the subject property, SELLER shall provide PURCHASER with an exclusive, irrevocable option to purchase that certain adjoining parcel of real property commonly known as  11400 S.E. 147th , Portland Oregon.  Said option shall be for no further or other consideration.  The terms of said option shall provide for a purchase price of said adjoining parcel in the amount of $240,000.00.  The option shall be exercised not sooner than October 1, 2002, nor later than November 30,  2004.  The purchase price for said adjoining parcel shall be paid in full at the closing established by the parties to complete the exercise of the option contemplated herein.

 Earnest money shall be deposited into escrow and applied towards the purchase price except as hereafter provided.  SELLER shall furnish at the sole expense of SELLER a title insurance policy insuring the PURCHASER of good and marketable title for the purchase price.  Prior to closing the transaction, the SELLER will furnish to the PURCHASER a preliminary title report made by a title insurance company showing the condition of the title to said property.  If the SELLER does not approve the sale, or cannot furnish marketable title within thirty days after the notice containing a written statement of the defects, or having approved the sale, fails to consummate the same, the earnest money herein receipted for shall be refunded.  If SELLER approves the sale and title is marketable and the PURCHASER fails to complete purchase as herein specified within thirty days of notice that escrow is ready to close, then the earnest money paid or agreed to be paid shall be forfeited and this agreement(contract) thereupon shall be of no further binding effect.

